  plaqueTitle: Traditional Ancestral Kuwako (Smoking Pipe)
  plaqueDescription: A handcrafted smoking pipe fashioned from dense indigenous hardwood
    and brass, historically smoked by tribal elders and community leaders during
    council meetings and peaceful negotiations.
  artifactInspectionDescription: Smooth polished hardwood bowl fitted with a curved
    stem and reinforced brass ferrule. Faint aromatic resin and charred tobacco residue
    line the interior bowl.
  initialDialogue: what should i do
  plaqueDialogue: what could this artifact be
  artifactDialogue: i wonder what this artifact looks like
